# Implementation Plan — Sprint 2: Data Integrity for Real Use

## Goal Description
Implement Sprint 2 per [CLUS_development_spec.md](file:///d:/Shahzaad/Projects/College/classroomUtilOpSystem/CLUS_development_spec.md), focusing on data integrity, cascade delete protections, automated audit trails, dynamic capacity validation triggers on updates, and full UI/API management for Departments and Courses.

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Key Decisions in Sprint 2:**
> 1. **Audit Columns**: `Course_Schedule` will include `created_by` (linking to `users.id`) and `updated_at` (auto-updated timestamp).
> 2. **Integrity Triggers**:
>    - `Course_Schedule` `BEFORE UPDATE`: prevents double-booking room/batch or assigning an oversized batch on schedule edits.
>    - `Room` `BEFORE UPDATE`: prevents reducing a room's capacity below any batch currently scheduled in it.
>    - `Batch` `BEFORE UPDATE`: prevents increasing a batch's student count above any room's capacity it is currently scheduled in.
> 3. **Cascade Impact Preview**: Before deleting a Department, Batch, or Room, the UI will query an impact preview endpoint (`/api/departments/:id/impact`, etc.) and present a modal detailing exact counts of dependent records (e.g., "Deleting Department CS will delete 4 courses, 3 batches, and 8 scheduled classes") before asking for explicit confirmation.
> 4. **Department & Course Management UI**: Dedicated tabs in the dashboard with full coordinator management (create, delete, list) and viewer read-only protection.

